ProjectivePoint -- Class of a projective point
**********************************************

Description
===========

A subclass of *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, mainly used for pretty printing.
Can be constructed using a *note projective variety:
(Varieties)ProjectiveVariety, plus a *note visible list:
(Macaulay2Doc)VisibleList,.

+-------------------------+
|i1 : P = Proj(QQ[x,y,z]);|
+-------------------------+
|i2 : pt = P(1,2,3)       |
|                         |
|o2 = (1 : 2 : 3)         |
|                         |
|o2 : ProjectivePoint     |
+-------------------------+
|i3 : pt == P{2,4,6}      |
|                         |
|o3 = true                |
+-------------------------+

Use ring to retrieve the coefficient field.

+------------+
|i4 : ring pt|
|            |
|o4 = QQ     |
|            |
|o4 : Ring   |
+------------+

Methods that use an object of class ProjectivePoint:
====================================================

  * "ProjectivePoint == ProjectivePoint"
  * "ring(ProjectivePoint)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note ProjectivePoint: ProjectivePoint, is a *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, <
*note VisibleList: (Macaulay2Doc)VisibleList, < *note BasicList:
(Macaulay2Doc)BasicList, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

