globalHeight -- Multiplicative height function
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        globalHeight pt
  * Inputs:
      * pt, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, representing homogeneous
        coordinates or an instance of the type *note ProjectivePoint:
        ProjectivePoint,
  * Outputs:
      * the multiplicative height function

Description
===========

This method computes the multiplicative height function given by
$(x_0:\dots:x_n)\mapsto \prod_{v}\max_i|x_i|_v ^{d_v/d}$. Over rational numbers
the result will be given as a precise value.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : globalHeight {1/1,2/3,5/8}                 |
|                                                |
|o1 = 24                                         |
|                                                |
|o1 : QQ                                         |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : PP = Proj(QQ[x,y,z]); pt = PP(1/1,2/3,5/8);|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : globalHeight pt                            |
|                                                |
|o4 = 24                                         |
|                                                |
|o4 : QQ                                         |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : F = toField(QQ[u]/(u^3-5));                |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : globalHeight {u,u^2/5,1_F}                 |
|                                                |
|o6 = 2.924017738212866                          |
|                                                |
|o6 : RR (of precision 53)                       |
+------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use globalHeight:
=========================

  * "globalHeight(List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note globalHeight: globalHeight, is a *note method function with
options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

