File: RationalPoints2.info, Node: integers, Next: hermiteNormalForm, Prev: charpoly, Up: Top

integers -- Compute a basis for the integers of a number field
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        integers F
        discriminant F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a number field
  * Outputs:
      * return an integral basis of the algebraic integers of the field F as a
        *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, and compute the discriminant

Description
===========

This is an implementation of the Zassenhaus' Round 2 algorithm, following the
textbook A course in computational algebraic number theory by Henri Cohen
(Algorithm 6.1.8). Given a number field $F=\mathbf Q(\theta)$ defined as a
simple extension over the rational numbers by an integral primitive element
$\theta$, it computes an integral basis of the algebraic integers, expressed as
polynomials in $\theta$.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : integers QQ                    |
|                                    |
|o1 = {1}                            |
|                                    |
|o1 : List                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : integers toField(QQ[i]/(i^2+1))|
|                                    |
|o2 = {1, i}                         |
|                                    |
|o2 : List                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : integers toField(QQ[a]/(a^2+3))|
|                                    |
|         1    1                     |
|o3 = {1, -a + -}                    |
|         2    2                     |
|                                    |
|o3 : List                           |
+------------------------------------+

The discriminant is computed using the same algorithm.

+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : discriminant toField(QQ[a]/(a^2+3))  |
|                                          |
|o4 = -3                                   |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : discriminant toField(QQ[a]/(a^4-a+2))|
|                                          |
|o5 = 2021                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

Ways to use integers:
=====================

  * "integers(Ring)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note integers: integers, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

